# STIG CD16-00-007300: PostgreSQL must provide a warning to appropriate support sta
# STIG ID: V-261919 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `pg16-cd16-00-007300-audit-space-warning-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `pg16`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CD16-00-007300: PostgreSQL must provide a warning to appropriate support staff when allocated au`
    description `PostgreSQL must provide a warning to appropriate support staff when allocated audit record storage volume reaches 75 percent of maximum audit record storage capacity.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `pg16,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CD16-00-007300,NIST-800-53:AU-5(1)`
    control_objective `AU-5(1)`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `dba`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `PostgreSQL16:localhost:pg-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for CD16-00-007300.`

    component_id `comp-pg16-db`

    impl_AU_5_1 `This control is validated by checking the required PostgreSQL configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT pg_param
        parameter `log_destination`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE param_state
        found boolean = true
        value string = `stderr`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN pg_config_param
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF param_state
            OBJECT_REF pg_param
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
